<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maurice Yaméogo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maurice Yaméogo was the first president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-volta">Upper Volta</a>, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a>, leading the territory to independence on 5 August 1960. He established a one-party state under his Voltaic Democratic Union. Austerity measures provoked strikes and mass protests in January 1966, and the army under Sangoulé Lamizana removed him from power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maurice-yameogo.jpg" alt="Maurice Yaméogo" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown, Service de Presse et d'Information. France. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maurice_Yam%C3%A9ogo,_1960_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
